 "purpose": "kin/physics3d's grab and climb (P2d) on the climb level (tests/climb_level.hpp): the skinned person (skinned_biped_walk.glb) is driven by a scripted timeline of commands (a hand takes hold or lets go, the reach direction, a move up or along the surface, a pull-up, a jump off, a drop) over a 4 m wall with a ledge on top, an overhang, a smooth wall with four holds and a lip, a platform that moves, a crate hung from, a wall of ice and a ledge under a low roof. The route and its checkpoints are in this file; tests/physics3d_traversal_tests.cpp runs the same route with no GPU and asserts the positions, modes and events. The character is an ECS entity (CharacterController3D with traversal on) animated by a locomotion Animator3D with the foot placer on the physics floor and a two-bone arm each on the anchors; the debug lines show the bodies, the grips (green held, yellow reaching, orange slipping: cross, surface normal, surface frame, line to the body), the hang place and what a free hand that is asked to grab can see (blue surfaces, magenta ledges with the top the pull-up goes to, white holds). No Cycles truth: the check is that two runs give the same picture byte for byte.",
